Janis Papanagnou wrote:

 > Blessed scroll of light will wake him up? - Wow! Learned something
 > new. My own tries to repeatedly play a bugle(!) did not work; but
 > switching on the light does. Great 8-)

I don't know the logic behind the light, maybe he just needs to see
you #-).

The scroll has to be blessed for its 9-square radius. This reaches
both potential MK positions from the upstairs. Uncursed scrolls or
wand/spell of light simply don't reach that far (5-square radius).

I think you can also kick at the air (or something) to wake him up.
This works with other quest nemeses (Chromatic Dragon for example),
but often requires multiple tries.

 > I have not so many darts, but also daggers, and crossbow bolts
 > (though yet unskilled [...]). I also do not have enchant weapon
 > scrolls.

You usually find a few dart/arrow traps you can disarm to get 100+
missile weapons. Or just use rocks. As I said, even +0 stuff kills
him eventually. Being unskilled doesn't really matter.

 > The main problem that I recall to have had with that approach - I
 > already did that in some other game before - is that Kaen jumps
 > around and often left the straight line-of-fire.

Well, just wait till he is in line-of-fire again #-). He might also
cast a healing spell or two at himself, but so far I always got him
sooner or later with this method.

 > [...] and probably enchant my yet unused gauntlets of dexterity.

With monks, I'd rather go with gauntlets of power. I'd even spend a
wish on them (only role where I'd do that). But I usually try to keep
my monks vegan/vegetarian these days which makes getting strength
difficult. If you eat meat (giants), GoP aren't important.

